o](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-community/meta#gitlab-duo)!\n\n*This message was [generated automatically](https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/infrastructure/engineering-productivity/triage-operations).\n[Improve it](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/quality/triage-ops/-/blob/master/triage/processor/community/thank_contribution.rb)\nor [delete it](https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/infrastructure/engineering-productivity/triage-operations/#reactive-delete_bot_comment-command).*","createdAt":"2026-10-11T19:25:18Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/db64e2b72f6b611e5c50086e9d6dfe846a774991","resolvable":false,"resolved":false,"resolvedBy":null},"id":"gid://gitlab/Note/3994147855","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-11T19:25:18Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3994147855"},{"author":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/1786152","username":"gitlab-bot"},"body":"\u003c!-- triage-serverless HackathonLabel --\u003e\nThis merge request is eligible for the October 2026 hackathon! :tada:\n\nTo earn points on the [Hackathon Leaderboard](https://contributors.gitlab.com/hackathon),\nsign in to contributors.gitlab.com/hackathon and accept the [hackathon rules](https://contributors.gitlab.com/docs/hackathon-rules)\nwhen prompted. Your contributions will not count towards the hackathon if you do not accept the hackathon rules.\nFailure to abide by the hackathon rules will disqualify you from the hackathon without warning.\n\n*This message was [generated automatically](https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/infrastructure/engineering-productivity/triage-operations).\n[Improve it](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/quality/triage-ops/-/blob/master/triage/processor/community/hackathon_label.rb)\nor [delete it](https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/infrastructure/engineering-productivity/triage-operations/#reactive-delete_bot_comment-command).*","createdAt":"2026-10-11T19:25:20Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/be56de445a72a349141244656bd59008c7392bb2","resolvable":false,"resolved":false,"resolvedBy":null},"id":"gid://gitlab/Note/3994147897","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-11T19:25:20Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3994147897"},{"author":{"bot":true,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/31177744","username":"contributors.gitlab.com"},"body":"Hey `@syedsaifalialvi`, thanks for helping label this merge request :pray:\n\n\n_Posted via [contributors.gitlab.com](https://contributors.gitlab.com)._","createdAt":"2026-10-11T19:28:11Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/991cb206a8ddf0b091e497c0bc8b95e03c0ba5bf","resolvable":false,"resolved":false,"resolvedBy":null},"id":"gid://gitlab/Note/3994152008","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-11T19:28:11Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3994152008"},{"author":{"bot":true,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/31177744","username":"contributors.gitlab.com"},"body":"Hey @syedsaifalialvi, thanks for requesting a review!\n\nFeel free to address any feedback by `@GitLabDuo`, or wait for another reviewer to validate it first!\n\nHey  :wave:\n\n- Do you have capacity and domain expertise to review this? If not, find one or more [reviewers](https://gitlab-org.gitlab.io/gitlab-roulette/) and assign to them.\n- If you've reviewed it, add the ~\"workflow::in dev\" label if these changes need more work before the next review.\n- Please ensure the group's Product Manager has validated the linked issue.\n\n\u003c!--\n@gitlab-bot ready @GitLabDuo\n--\u003e\n\n\n\n_Posted via [contributors.gitlab.com](https://contributors.gitlab.com)._","createdAt":"2026-10-11T19:28:37Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/47d0b9bbc1c72c3f6306ca54d57fb90d29658b12","resolvable":true,"resolved":true,"resolvedBy":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/11334402","username":"ahmed.hemdan"}},"id":"gid://gitlab/DiscussionNote/3994152499","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-12T13:04:42Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3994152499"},{"author":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/1786152","username":"gitlab-bot"},"body":"`@GitLabDuo`, this ~\"Community contribution\" is ready for review.\n\n- Do you have capacity and domain expertise to review this? If not, find one or more [reviewers](https://gitlab-org.gitlab.io/gitlab-roulette/) and assign to them.\n- If you've reviewed it, add the ~\"workflow::in dev\" label if these changes need more work before the next review.\n- Please ensure the group's Product Manager has validated the linked issue.\n\n*This message was [generated automatically](https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/infrastructure/engineering-productivity/triage-operations).\n[Improve it](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/quality/triage-ops/-/blob/master/triage/processor/community/command_mr_request_review.rb)\nor [delete it](https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/infrastructure/engineering-productivity/triage-operations/#reactive-delete_bot_comment-command).*","createdAt":"2026-10-11T19:28:45Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/47d0b9bbc1c72c3f6306ca54d57fb90d29658b12","resolvable":true,"resolved":true,"resolvedBy":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/11334402","username":"ahmed.hemdan"}},"id":"gid://gitlab/DiscussionNote/3994152676","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-12T13:04:42Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3994152676"},{"author":{"bot":true,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/21826781","username":"GitLabDuo"},"body":"The change is a small, correct cleanup. It removes `--opened` from the issue and incident list examples and points the `mr note` help at the `resolve` and `reopen` subcommands. The only issue I raised is minor: the rewritten `Long` paragraph in `mr_note.go` is still hard-wrapped across two source lines.\n\n1 finding (1 minor) across 1 file:\n\n**Minor**\n- command-documentation: `internal/commands/mr/note/mr_note.go:28`","createdAt":"2026-10-11T19:29:49Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/4e3ec8197bc233dffaf7767be237fa371bda9f41","resolvable":false,"resolved":false,"resolvedBy":null},"id":"gid://gitlab/Note/3994154013","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-11T19:29:49Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3994154013"},{"author":{"bot":true,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/21826781","username":"GitLabDuo"},"body":"**[Minor] command-documentation**\n\nThe `Long` paragraph is still hard-wrapped across two source lines. Cobra emits `Long` verbatim, so the terminal shows an orphan line break. The project's help-text rule says each paragraph should be one source line. You rewrote both lines here, so this is a good time to join them. The new test collapses whitespace with `strings.Fields`, so it would still pass after the change. The generated `docs/source/mr/note/_index.md` would also need regenerating with `make gen-docs`.","createdAt":"2026-10-11T19:29:50Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/9fc13295df64ad930e44d68b76323cc20a81c798","resolvable":true,"resolved":true,"resolvedBy":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/11334402","username":"ahmed.hemdan"}},"id":"gid://gitlab/DiffNote/3994154021","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-12T13:04:29Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":{"filePath":"internal/commands/mr/note/mr_note.go","newLine":28,"oldLine":null},"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3994154021"},{"author":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/21230898","username":"syedsaifalialvi"},"body":"Good point, keeping it in single line is better","createdAt":"2026-10-11T19:32:44Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/9fc13295df64ad930e44d68b76323cc20a81c798","resolvable":true,"resolved":true,"resolvedBy":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/11334402","username":"ahmed.hemdan"}},"id":"gid://gitlab/DiffNote/3994158711","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-12T13:04:29Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":{"filePath":"internal/commands/mr/note/mr_note.go","newLine":28,"oldLine":null},"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3994158711"},{"author":{"bot":true,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/31177744","username":"contributors.gitlab.com"},"body":"Hey @syedsaifalialvi, thanks for requesting a review!\n\nHey @ahmed.hemdan :wave:\n\n- Do you have capacity and domain expertise to review this? If not, find one or more [reviewers](https://gitlab-org.gitlab.io/gitlab-roulette/) and assign to them.\n- If you've reviewed it, add the ~\"workflow::in dev\" label if these changes need more work before the next review.\n- Please ensure the group's Product Manager has validated the linked issue.\n\n\n\n_Posted via [contributors.gitlab.com](https://contributors.gitlab.com)._","createdAt":"2026-10-11T19:34:53Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/13c20255fe43ad6f49ed778a0fb94154f56a9d4f","resolvable":true,"resolved":true,"resolvedBy":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/11334402","username":"ahmed.hemdan"}},"id":"gid://gitlab/DiscussionNote/3994163220","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-12T13:04:38Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3994163220"},{"author":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/11334402","username":"ahmed.hemdan"},"body":"**suggestion (non-blocking):** Can we use `cmdtest.SetupCmdForTest` here and `cmd.SetOut(f.IO().StdOut)` to capture help?\n\n```suggestion:-3+2\n\t\texec := cmdtest.SetupCmdForTest(t, func(f cmdutils.Factory) *cobra.Command {\n\t\t\tcmd := NewCmdNote(f)\n\t\t\tcmd.SetOut(f.IO().StdOut)\n\t\t\treturn cmd\n\t\t}, false)\n\n\t\toutput, err := exec(\"--help\")\n\t\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n```\n\nAlso the same in `internal/commands/issuable/list/issuable_list_test.go` in **line 65**.","createdAt":"2026-10-12T13:05:23Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/7c66416734b982e0fbb6e1bcd3a8cf40b086d11e","resolvable":true,"resolved":true,"resolvedBy":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/21230898","username":"syedsaifalialvi"}},"id":"gid://gitlab/DiffNote/3998265436","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-12T13:13:28Z","lastEditedBy":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/11334402","username":"ahmed.hemdan"},"position":{"filePath":"internal/commands/mr/note/mr_note_test.go","newLine":37,"oldLine":null},"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3998265436"},{"author":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/11334402","username":"ahmed.hemdan"},"body":"@syedsaifalialvi Thank you for your contribution! :pray_tone2:\n\nLeft one non-blocking comment on the test helper, otherwise LGTM! :white_check_mark:","createdAt":"2026-10-12T13:05:24Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/d6b8007dac4c7869d9ecaa606f27742cbdea6c24","resolvable":true,"resolved":true,"resolvedBy":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/11334402","username":"ahmed.hemdan"}},"id":"gid://gitlab/DiscussionNote/3998265484","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-19T06:13:01Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3998265484"},{"author":{"bot":true,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/21826781","username":"GitLabDuo"},"body":"The change is correct and small. The earlier hard-wrap point is fixed, since the paragraph is now one source line and the docs were regenerated. The one remaining issue is style: the `Long` field uses an interpreted string with `\\n` rather than the raw-string heredoc form the project asks for. It is a quick fix.\n\n1 finding (1 minor) across 1 file:\n\n**Minor**\n- command-documentation: `internal/commands/mr/note/mr_note.go:26`","createdAt":"2026-10-12T13:07:51Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/2221a12221028a7dead41819eb92ebfffc4903da","resolvable":false,"resolved":false,"resolvedBy":null},"id":"gid://gitlab/Note/3998281922","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-12T13:07:51Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3998281922"},{"author":{"bot":true,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/21826781","username":"GitLabDuo"},"body":"**[Minor] command-documentation**\n\nThis `Long` is built from an interpreted string with an embedded `\\n` instead of a raw-string heredoc. The project's help-text rule asks for `heredoc.Docf` with a raw string block, one source line per paragraph. The one-line paragraph is correct, but the quoted literal with `\\n` is the pattern the rule forbids, and other commands don't use it. Could you switch to the raw-string form? It renders the same, so the new test and the generated docs stay valid.\n```suggestion:-0+0\n\t\tLong: heredoc.Docf(`\n\t\t\tCreates a comment by default. Use %[1]sglab mr note resolve%[1]s to resolve a discussion or %[1]sglab mr note reopen%[1]s to reopen one.\n\t\t`, \"`\"),\n```","createdAt":"2026-10-12T13:07:52Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/5927c19f977b350722be6e56432212550cc1316e","resolvable":true,"resolved":true,"resolvedBy":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/21230898","username":"syedsaifalialvi"}},"id":"gid://gitlab/DiffNote/3998282043","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-15T04:24:03Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":{"filePath":"internal/commands/mr/note/mr_note.go","newLine":26,"oldLine":null},"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_3998282043"},{"author":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/21230898","username":"syedsaifalialvi"},"body":"Thank you @ahmed.hemdan  :smile:\n\nI have applied your suggestion as well,","createdAt":"2026-10-17T06:43:08Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/d6b8007dac4c7869d9ecaa606f27742cbdea6c24","resolvable":true,"resolved":true,"resolvedBy":{"bot":false,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/11334402","username":"ahmed.hemdan"}},"id":"gid://gitlab/DiscussionNote/4034163555","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-19T06:13:01Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_4034163555"},{"author":{"bot":true,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/21826781","username":"GitLabDuo"},"body":":warning: @syedsaifalialvi, you don't have permission to create a pipeline for Code Review Flow in this project. Contact your administrator to update your permissions.\n\nError code: [DCR4003](https://gitlab.com/help/user/duo_agent_platform/flows/foundational_flows/code_review/troubleshooting.md#error-dcr4003)","createdAt":"2026-10-17T07:17:09Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/68f4534ef0b17e4d628ff003c597c205869a4e34","resolvable":false,"resolved":false,"resolvedBy":null},"id":"gid://gitlab/Note/4034213975","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-17T07:17:09Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":null,"url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/merge_requests/4077#note_4034213975"},{"author":{"bot":true,"id":"gid://gitlab/User/21826781","username":"GitLabDuo"},"body":"I finished my review and found nothing to comment on. Nice work! :tada:\n\n- Both earlier threads on `mr_note.go` are fixed. `Long` is now a single-line paragraph inside `heredoc.Docf`, and `docs/source/mr/note/_index.md` matches it.\n- The `--opened` example is removed from the shared issue and incident list help in `issuable_list.go`. Both generated docs pages match. The flag itself stays registered but hidden, so existing usage still works.\n- The new help tests use `cmdtest.SetupCmdForTest` and assert on user-visible `--help` output. This follows the repo conventions and covers both the issue and incident variants.\n- I found no new correctness, security or convention problems in the test and doc changes.\n- My checkout still showed the old `--opened` example on `issuable_list.go` line 90. I reviewed that file from the diff, which shows the line removed.","createdAt":"2026-10-18T10:47:42Z","discussion":{"id":"gid://gitlab/Discussion/0367b1688242adc58fc586020663c266be2485b4","resolvable":false,"resolved":false,"resolvedBy":null},"id":"gid://gitlab/Note/4037394717","lastEditedAt":"2026-10-18T10:47:42Z","lastEditedBy":null,"position":nul